          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness observes around twenty red-orange colored, spherical objects. The objects disappear behind the houses in the village. The witness thinks they might be Thai lanterns but is unfamiliar with the phenomenon. The observation of orange balls in the sky on a weekend night evokes Thai lanterns. The near absence of wind makes it difficult to correlate the movement of the objects with that of the wind. The lack of other witnesses or reports in the press or on the internet does not allow this hypothesis, though extremely likely, to be confirmed. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of released Thai lanterns following a private party.",
